    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "...it feels like a heavy burden, but it's the only thing that feels real anymore. There's a certain kind of honor in it, isn't there? To not run away, to not just live on as a coward while their families go without. To face the debt head-on, without any more excuses or empty promises of 'making it right'. Just a final, quiet end to the shame.",
